<section class="v3-prose">
  <div class="v3-wrap">
    <p><em>Last updated: 12 October 2026</em></p>

    <p>{{ site.company.legalName }} (UEN {{ site.company.uen }}) ("we", "us") operates Nexus POS, a point-of-sale app
    for shops, cafés and restaurants. We follow Singapore's Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (PDPA). This policy covers
    business owners and staff who use the Nexus POS app, and their customers who order through a Nexus QR menu.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your account:</strong> the name, mobile number and email address you sign up with.</li>
      <li><strong>Your business:</strong> business details, address, tax settings, menu and prices, staff logins,
      tables, and the sales and order records you create.</li>
      <li><strong>Menu photos you choose to read:</strong> the photos are sent to our menu-reading service to pull out
      items and prices. We do not keep the photos. We keep only the draft menu, the time you confirmed it is your own
      menu, and what the reading cost.</li>
      <li><strong>Your customers' orders:</strong> the table, items and order details your customers send through your
      QR menu.</li>
      <li><strong>Crash reports:</strong> when the app hits an error it can send us a report. The report holds the error
      type, a masked message, the stack trace, the app version, the operating system and the device model. It holds no
      personal details, yours or your customers'.</li>
      <li><strong>Service logs:</strong> when the app talks to our servers we log the time, the IP address, the action
      and the result. We use these logs to keep the service secure and working.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not collect payment card details. The app records cash and PayNow payments that you take at the
    counter.</p>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <p>We use this data to run your account and your till, to send sign-in codes, and to read menu photos into your
    menu. We also use it to print receipts, kitchen tickets and table QR slips, to show your sales, and to keep the
    service secure and fix faults. We do not sell personal data or use it for advertising. The app contains no
    advertising or tracking.</p>

    <h2>Who processes it for us</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Railway</strong>: hosting for our servers and database.</li>
      <li><strong>Bird</strong>: sends WhatsApp sign-in codes. WhatsApp (Meta) delivers them.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong>: sends sign-in codes by email.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: reads menu photos (Workers AI) and delivers product images.</li>
      <li><strong>Backblaze</strong>: stores product images.</li>
      <li><strong>Grafana Labs</strong>: holds service logs in Singapore for 14 days.</li>
      <li><strong>Expo</strong>: delivers app updates. It sees your device's IP address and app version when the app
      checks for an update.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Crash reports go to our own error-tracking server, which runs on our hosting. No third party receives them.</p>
    <p>Some of these providers process data outside Singapore. We use providers that are bound to protect it to a
    standard comparable to the PDPA.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We keep your data while your account is open. To delete your account and its business data, go to
    <strong>Settings → Account → Delete account</strong> in the app. This removes the business and its records from
    our database, except records we must keep by law. Product images are stored separately. Email us and we will
    erase them. Service logs are deleted after 14 days.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see or correct the personal data we hold about you, and you can withdraw your consent. Email
    <a href="mailto:{{ site.company.email }}">{{ site.company.email }}</a>.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Nexus POS is a business tool. It is not meant for children.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We will post any change on this page and update the date above.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
